<title>SOUTH AFRICA: STERLING SINKS INTO YEAR LOSS, NO DIV.</title>
<headline>STERLING SINKS INTO YEAR LOSS, NO DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     20.0 loss   vs 0.7 profit</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.88 loss   vs 0.13 profit</p>
<p>    Operating loss	  1.72 loss   vs 2.28 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.19	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   2.35	  vs 2.15</p>
<p>    Turnover		  41.72	 vs 52.01</p>
<p>Full name: Sterling Clothing Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said the local clothing industry had</p>
<p>experienced its worst ever year due to industrial action and </p>
<p>increasing volumes of illegal imports.</p>
<p>The firm added that due to the seasonal nature of the</p>
<p>business a return to profitability was not foreseen for the</p>
<p>first six months of the current year, but the group does expect</p>
<p>to post a full year profit.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
